<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Starting point for apps whose stage behaviour is known.

	type 0 ("iPad") lets an app resize live, which is what Split View and
	backgrounding need; apps left out of this file default to type 1 ("iPhone")
	and relaunch instead, because that is the safe behaviour for anything whose
	layout has not been checked.

	disabled hides an app from the picker entirely: either it refuses to run in
	a hosted scene, or it owns hardware (camera, sensors) that makes a half
	height window pointless.

	Everything here is overridable per app in Settings; these are only defaults.
-->
